      "title": "EC249A",
      "description": "EC249A - International Finance (Winter 2027) Job Details | Wilfrid Laurier University Skip to main content Home Page About Us Why Join Our Team How to apply Career Opportunities Academic Positions Staff and Management Positions View All Positions Join Talent Community Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Home Page About Us Why Join Our Team How to apply Career Opportunities Academic Positions Staff and Management Positions View All Positions Join Talent Community Sign Into My Profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: EC249A - International Finance (Winter 2027) Apply now » Date: Sep 30, 2026 Location: Waterloo, CA Company: Wilfrid Laurier University Faculty/Academic Area: Lazaridis School of Bus. & Econ. Department : Lazaridis Economics Campus: Waterloo Employee Group: WLUFA Requisition ID: 11881 Position Title: EC249A – International Finance (Winter 2027) Term: Winter 2027 (January 1 – April 30) Days/Times: Tues/Thurs. 4:00 – 5:20 pm Hours per week/Hours Total: 3 per week/36 total Mode of Delivery: In-Person Type of Course: Lecture Anticipated Class Size: 100 Additional Course Requirements: None Posted on: September 30, 2026 Posting ends: October 15, 2026 Position Summary: This course is an introduction to issues in international finance. Topics may include international financial institutions, the balance of payments, exchange rates, international borrowing and lending and their relationship to international trade and the domestic economy. Qualifications – Required: Master’s degree Qualifications – Discipline: Economics Qualifications – Preferred: Teaching experience at the University level; PhD; Graduate studies or recent research relevant to the course. Salary: $10,212.40 Application Deadline: October 15, 2026 Submit with Application: Required for All Applicants CV (required) Candidate Application Form (CAF) Required